## Install

**macOS / Linux**

```sh
curl -fsSL https://krishj.com/ifseen/install.sh | sh
# or: brew install krishjoshi/tap/ifseen
```

**Windows** (PowerShell)

```powershell
irm https://krishj.com/ifseen/install.ps1 | iex
# or: scoop bucket add krishjoshi https://github.com/KrishJoshi/scoop-bucket; scoop install ifseen
```

**Python** (includes the optional free offline `local` provider via `[local]`)

```sh
pipx install "ifseen[all]==$version"
```

**Docker** (cameras, snapshot URLs and files; no screen or mic in a container)

```sh
docker run --rm -e GEMINI_API_KEY ghcr.io/krishjoshi/ifseen:$version --help
```

**Home Assistant**: add `https://github.com/$repo` as an add-on repository
([one click](https://my.home-assistant.io/redirect/supervisor_add_addon_repository/?repository_url=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2FKrishJoshi%2Fifseen)).
The add-on pulls a prebuilt image for amd64 / aarch64.

**JavaScript / TypeScript**: `npm install ifseen@$version`

The standalone binaries below bundle the screen, camera, mic and MQTT extras (not the
torch-based `local` provider). They're unsigned: macOS may need
`xattr -d com.apple.quarantine ./ifseen` (the install script does this for you), and Windows
SmartScreen may ask you to click **More info > Run anyway**. On Linux the mic needs
PortAudio (`sudo apt install libportaudio2`). Verify downloads with `SHA256SUMS`.
